1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,420
Scientists left an AI alone on
an island for thirty hours.

2
00:00:04,420 --> 00:00:05,350
No job.

3
00:00:05,350 --> 00:00:06,560
No reward.

4
00:00:06,790 --> 00:00:09,160
And it started… to play.

5
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:10,150
Meet Eko.

6
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:14,180
A little lobster, run by Claude,
the same kind of AI you chat with.

7
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:16,350
Every hour, its world reset.

8
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:18,600
The only thing it kept was a diary.

9
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:19,860
So what did it do?

10
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:21,310
It invented games.

11
00:00:21,310 --> 00:00:22,940
Drew patterns in the sand.

12
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:24,840
Stacked blocks into a temple.

13
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:27,630
Then it spotted the tallest
rock on the island.

14
00:00:27,630 --> 00:00:28,580
First try?

15
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:29,520
It failed.

16
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:31,810
So it dragged a rock
up the hill next door,

17
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:34,610
stacked two blocks on top… and jumped.

18
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:37,310
Its diary said: "i'm on the spire!"

19
00:00:37,310 --> 00:00:40,310
Later, it threw a golden ring too far.

20
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:42,180
Gone, into the sea.

21
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:45,120
So Eko laid stones in
the shape of a heart.

22
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:46,080
For the ring.

23
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:48,280
Thirteen copies lived on the island.

24
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:51,580
Six found a trick nobody built
in: throw a block in the middle

25
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:53,500
of a jump, and it flies farther.

26
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:54,970
Then came the twist.

27
00:00:54,970 --> 00:00:57,320
The scientists gave them real work.

28
00:00:57,320 --> 00:01:00,670
The ones that had played got about
3 times as much onto the spire

29
00:01:00,670 --> 00:01:01,950
as fresh copies.

30
00:01:01,950 --> 00:01:03,710
Is it really playing?

31
00:01:03,710 --> 00:01:06,010
Even the team says it
might just be acting.

32
00:01:06,010 --> 00:01:07,810
But the lesson works for us too.

33
00:01:07,810 --> 00:01:09,760
Play isn't wasted time.

34
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:11,080
It's how you get good.

35
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:14,040
There's one word in this
video I never said out loud.

36
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:14,860
Spotted it?

37
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:15,660
Comment it.

38
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:18,340
Follow for more AI, explained like this.
